R2-274: the repeat floor is not zero on a glass wall, so the control limit is measured

Two renders of the SAME build at f2978 differ on 2-14 % of the pixels of the
east wall's regions at a 1/255 threshold -- the wall is transmissive and
specular, adaptive sampling and the denoiser do not repeat, and R2-150's
0.00 % repeat floor was measured on asphalt. At 8/255 the floor is 0.000 % in
every control region and 0.131 % in the wound.

So the negative-control verdict is taken at 8/255 against 3x the MEASURED
floor, never against zero. Charging a control with a change the renderer makes
against itself is how a correct fix gets rejected.
